he dji om4  is the magnetic grip it has truly  changed it from the om3  and made it a better upgraded device the  magnetic grip comes off so quickly and  so easily  i personally use the grip clamp around  the phone because i don't like  sticking anything to the back of my  phone and using that magnetic clamp  i'd much rather use the simple pull-on  pull-off grip  and then i can use it whenever i want  and store it whenever i don't need it  all you have to remember is to align the  two white dots  when you're connecting the magnets  together and it will be absolutely  perfect  the app does actually tell you when you  haven't aligned the two dots  and when you have to realign it so if  you ever aren't 100  sure you will get told and it makes it  very user-friendly  talking about the technology of the  device and the integration with the  mobile app  some of the auto focusing features are  actually really good  the simple fact that you can click the  trigger just once and it will  automatically grab onto somebody's face  and automatically track that person  without you having to do  anything technical without you having to  draw that person's face on your screen  or literally anything at all makes it a  great  upgrade and a great feature i think one  of the downsides to this however  is it does pivot and change very quickly  especially if that person's moving very  fast  or if any subject in that shot is moving  very fast so it does make it a little  bit unstable  it can also sometimes grab the  completely wrong thing  for example i was trying to capture an  individual today and instead of  capturing them  it captured the printer i i can't  explain that one at all  but it just did so sometimes it won't  capture  what you're trying to connect to and it  will just  malfunction like technology does every  now and again as an architect obviously  i always criticized the design of  something and it wouldn't be  my way if i didn't criticize at least  one error  that i personally see in this device the  button placement is  actually really really good my only  concern  is the zoom button feature it is just  slightly too high to be able to grab  properly with your thumb  so i think it would have been nice if it  was located a little bit lower  and also the very simple fact that the  usbc port is completely exposed to the  elements  talking about negative features as well  the tripod that it comes with  is well one great that it comes with a  free tripod but two is a little bit  cheap and nasty the whole gimbal itself  is built quite well and quite solid  however  the tripod itself is very very cheap  plastic  so now we need to talk about the actual  performance of the gimbal and is  it any good well i tested it out today  and i've tested it out in practice  and it does everything that your proper  big dslr gimbal can do  just as well sometimes a little bit  worse but we'll get to that in a minute  so overall it gets very very smooth  shots it's very easy to control  and it works very similar to the big  gimbals the three axis gimbals that  you'd be used to on a dslr if you've  ever used a big dslr gimbal it is a very  simple  transition to a mobile gimbal if you  haven't it is a bit of a learning curve  before you understand  how the mechanism and the gimbals and  axis work themselves from a negative  point of view though  it does struggle to get the front direct  shots so if you're coming very low to  the bottom of the table and going closer  to a product for example  it does struggle to really tilt the  phone 90 degrees  against that gimbal itself so the only  workaround i've found so far is to tip  the whole gimbal upside down  to be able to use it properly this isn't  the worst thing in the world but i guess  there's definitely some more  improvements that they can work on in  the future  now i just want to quickly point out  this jumper is super warm and super  comfortable  not sponsored not paid for but there is  a link down below if you want to check  it out because it just genuinely is a  very very comfortable jumper  now there is a very simple and very  logical reason why i purchased the om4  over the om3  especially considering the om3 is half  the price of the im4  and it is a simple fact that the om4 has  a 230 gram weight capacity whereas the  om-3  only has a 200 gram capacity i  personally use  a samsung galaxy s20 ultra which comes  in at 226 grams  so i cannot use the om3 unfortunately it  has to be the om4  however having said this if you do have  a phone that comes  in under that 200 gram category i think  it might even be 210  i'll put a little snippet here because i  can't remember off top my head  then you are more than welcome to grab  the om3 it is a great purchase at an  exceptional price at the moment okay so  why at the start of this video did i say  every single architect needs a gimbal  and especially this one  well to be honest you don't need this  gimbal in particular  but you do need some sort of gimbal  mobile phones are getting  more and more advanced and obviously it  is becoming harder and harder to stand  out on social media  everybody is looking to build their own  brand their own business  their own whatever and it is becoming  very hard to do this in 2020  especially now that we're entering a  whole new 2021  where people haven't been able to travel  for 12 months they're eager to get out  and there's going to be so much mass  content produced in a short period of  time  i think it's critical now more so than  ever that you understand  personal branding and truly build up  your own presence  on your social media platforms and  personally i think there's only one way  to do it and that's through video  content  i think video content is the most  powerful the most interactive  and the most genuine form of social  media content that you can create right  now  not only that but videos are showcased  to a lot more people the algorithm  prefers them  and they just genuinely engage better  with people so to be able to create  good content and good videos you do  unfortunately need some sort of gimbal  to be able to create  that cinematography that everybody is  looking for if you're just walking  around using your phone  scrolling around you know taking videos  one it's gonna be  very very jumpy two it's gonna look  amateur as  and three you're just never gonna get  the shots that you're really truly  looking to get especially if you're  aspiring to create  like some of the best youtubers out  there that are creating some incredible  content  every single day anyway that's all from  me today guys thanks so much for  watching  i hope you enjoyed the video i hope you  got some good quality information out of  it if you did  make sure you smash that like button  down below help this video with  the youtube algorithm and if you want to  see more of my videos smash that  subscribe button down below  because as always i will see you next  monday
 

